# Example: calling methods

Receiver required. Parentheses and commas on arguments. PlayArea is Rect, so area lives on playArea.rect.

## Schema

```
Game = PlayArea Ball
PlayArea = Rect
Rect = Int/x Int/y Int/width Int/height
Ball = Int/x Int/y Int/dx Int/dy Int/rad
```

## Construction

```
[:Game
  [:PlayArea [0 0 800 600]]
  [:Ball 100 100 1 1 5]
]
```

## Methods

```
Rect::area = { width * height }

Rect::contains = {px, py | (px >= x) and (px <= (x + width)) and (py >= y) and (py <= (y + height))}

Ball::move = { [:Ball (x + dx) (y + dy) dx dy rad] }

Ball::step = { this.move() }

Game::playAreaSize = { playArea.rect.area() }

Game::ballInside = { playArea.rect.contains(ball.x, ball.y) }
```

## Target

```
%main
public static function main():Void {
    var assemblage = gameFactory();
    var helper = new WCHNTHelper();
    trace(assemblage.toConstruction(0, helper));
    trace("playAreaSize");
    trace(assemblage.playAreaSize());
    trace("ballInside");
    trace(assemblage.ballInside());
}
```
